# The build context for build/tools.Dockerfile. BuildKit reads the ignore
# file named after the Dockerfile in preference to the root .dockerignore,
# so this image's context is what this image needs and the other two
# images' contexts are unchanged by the tool sources this one compiles
# (#597: four gitignored tool binaries rode into both contexts, and the
# allow-list below is the shape that fix chose).
#
# Same allow-list as the root file and for the same reason: everything is
# excluded and only what `go build ./tools/<name>/` reads is admitted, so
# the next file added at the root stays out until someone admits it (#594,
# #597). `cmd` is not admitted, because no tool imports it.
#
# The re-includes are directories rather than globs, as at the root: a
# `*.go` allow-list would drop an embedded asset — internal/agent
# embeds ego.md — and break the build. The cost of admitting `tools`
# whole is that a contributor who has run `make build-tools` transfers
# the four executables it wrote there into this context. They are bloat
# and never ship: build/tools.Dockerfile compiles into /out and copies
# nothing from tools/<name>/<name>.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!internal
!tools

# Final deny, placed after the re-includes because the last matching
# pattern wins: a credential stays out of the context whatever a later
# re-include admits (#594).
.env
.env.*
